course: dictionary
lesson: 8869
title: Shortage: not having enough
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A shortage is when there is not enough of something that people need. Think of it as the gap between what is needed and what there is. If a class needs 30 pencils and there are only 25, there is a shortage of 5 pencils.
explain: Look for clue words near the word. The phrases «a shortage of», «water shortage» and «food shortages» all tell you that something is missing. Ask yourself: is something needed but not there? If yes, shortage is the right meaning.
explain: Test your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «A shortage of teachers» can become «not enough teachers», and the sentence still makes sense. That tells you the meaning is right.
fact: Shortage is a noun: one shortage, many shortages.
fact: «Shortage» means not having enough of something that is needed.
fact: «In short supply» means there is only a little of something, so it is hard to get.
fact: «A water shortage» happens when there is not enough water, for example in a drought.
fact: «A shortage of tiny computer chips in 2021 stopped car factories around the world.» One small missing part can stop many things from being made.
exercise: «A shortage of tiny computer chips stopped car factories around the world.» What does shortage mean here? | *Not enough of something that was needed | A factory that makes chips very quickly | Far too many chips in every shop | A new kind of car
exercise: What does «food shortages» mean? | Food sent by boat | Lots of food at every meal | Food cooked at home | *Not enough food
exercise: «Our school has a shortage of nurses this year.» What does this mean? | *There are not enough nurses for the job | There are too many nurses in the school | The school is closed for a week | Nurses are learning to swim
test: Which phrase means there is only a little of something, so it is hard to get? | Plenty to go round | *In short supply | Sad and glum | Very long
test: What can people do to help during a water shortage? | Waste it on the garden | Fill the bath to the top | Leave the taps running all day | *Save water
exam: Which word means «not enough of something that is needed»? | Plenty | Spare | Surplus | *Shortage
